WEBVTT

NOTE
Transcribed from the narration in this video. Every figure the
speaker states matches the OECD time-use data behind this page.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.740
Hola!

2
00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:02.580
You want to know about my day?

3
00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.840
Okay, but I'll have to tell
you while I'm on the move.

4
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.060
Personal care?

5
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.340
10 hours and 6 minutes.

6
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.540
That's 59 minutes less
than the global average.

7
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.300
Sleep, a shower,
meals, I keep it quick.

8
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.340
Then I work.

9
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.520
5 hours and 49 minutes of paid work.

10
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.680
That's over an hour more than
the average professional.

11
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.900
And at home?

12
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:29.380
Another 4 hours and 16
minutes of unpaid work.

13
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.440
Together, that's over 10 hours.

14
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.140
The heaviest workload
in all 35 countries.

15
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:42.220
In Mexico, women do 201 minutes
more unpaid work a day than men.

16
00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:47.720
That's 5 hours and 49 minutes
against just 2.5 for men.

17
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:48.780
Leisure?

18
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.720
Only 3 hours and 23 minutes.

19
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:56.200
Norway gets 2.5 hours more
than me every single day.

20
00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.600
That's a 38 day gap every year.

21
00:00:58.680 --> 00:00:59.800
And retirement?

22
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.820
Still waiting, until about 71.

23
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.100
That is the second latest
exit of all 35 countries.

24
00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.000
That's my day in Mexico.

25
00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.021
Hasta luego!
